        "content": "{\"formal\": {\"statement\": \"open Topology Filter in\\n∀ (f : ℕ → ℕ)\\n(hfpos : ∀ n, f n > 0)\\n(hfinc : StrictMonoOn f (Set.Ici 1))\\n(hf2 : f 2 = 2)\\n(hfmn : ∀ m n, m > 0 → n > 0 → IsRelPrime m n → f (m * n) = f m * f n), ∀ n > 0, f n = n\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"supporting_declarations\": [], \"rendered\": \"∀ (f : (ℕ → ℕ)),\\n  ((∀ (n : ℕ), ((f n) > 0)) →\\n    ((StrictMonoOn f (Set.Ici 1)) →\\n      (((f 2) = 2) →\\n        ((∀ (m n : ℕ), ((m > 0) → ((n > 0) → ((IsRelPrime m n) → ((f (m * n)) = ((f m) * (f n))))))) →\\n          (∀ n > 0, ((f n) = n))))))\"}, \"signature\": \"(f : ℕ → ℕ)\\n(hfpos : ∀ n, f n > 0)\\n(hfinc : StrictMonoOn f (Set.Ici 1))\\n(hf2 : f 2 = 2)\\n(hfmn : ∀ m n, m > 0 → n > 0 → IsRelPrime m n → f (m * n) = f m * f n)\\n: ∀ n > 0, f n = n\", \"informal\": \"Let $\\\\{f(n)\\\\}$ be a strictly increasing sequence of positive integers such that $f(2)=2$ and $f(mn)=f(m)f(n)$ for every relatively prime pair of positive integers $m$ and $n$ (the greatest common divisor of $m$ and $n$ is equal to $1$). Prove that $f(n)=n$ for every positive integer $n$.\", \"docstring\": \"/--\\nLet $\\\\{f(n)\\\\}$ be a strictly increasing sequence of positive integers such that $f(2)=2$ and $f(mn)=f(m)f(n)$ for every relatively prime pair of positive integers $m$ and $n$ (the greatest common divisor of $m$ and $n$ is equal to $1$). Prove that $f(n)=n$ for every positive integer $n$.\\n-/\", \"prechecks\": {\"status\": \"completed\", \"hints\": [{\"kind\": \"natural_arithmetic_review\", \"status\": \"advisory\"}], \"vacuity\": \"unresolved\"}, \"advisory\": {\"paraphrase_status\": \"completed\", \"differences\": [\"Formal vs. conversational language\", \"Detailed vs. concise conditions\", \"Conclusion phrasing variation\"], \"paraphrase\": \"For all functions f from natural numbers to natural numbers, if f is strictly increasing on the set of natural numbers greater than or equal to 1, always outputs positive natural numbers, satisfies f(2) = 2, and is multiplicative over coprime arguments, then for all natural numbers greater than 0, f(n) equals n.\", \"comparison_status\": \"completed\"}}"
      }
